        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alvin, Richard Farnsworth, Rose, Sissy Spacek, Dick Van Dyke, Edward G. Robinson, Jerry Paris, Wiley Harker\n- Films: The Straight Story, Never a Dull Moment, Things to Do in Denver When You're Dead\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n\nFacts:\n- Never a Dull Moment is a 1968 American comedy crime film from Walt Disney Productions that stars Dick Van Dyke and Edward G. Robinson and was directed by Jerry Paris.\n- In The Straight Story, Alvin is an elderly World War II veteran portrayed by Richard Farnsworth.\n- In The Straight Story, Alvin lives with his daughter Rose, who is portrayed by Sissy Spacek as a kind woman with an intellectual disability.\n- Wiley Harker appeared in the films Things to Do in Denver When You're Dead and The Straight Story.",
